# demo-video transcript template — the Claude turn `claude-delegate.cast` appends (Issue #2380)
#
# One Claude Code session turn in the JSONL dialect
# src/lib/hooks/sources/claude/transcript.ts reads: the operator's prompt
# (`origin.kind: human`, `promptSource: typed` — the markers #2196 requires
# before a `user` row is written), an assistant record that calls Bash with
# `commandmate ask …`, the `tool_result` for it, and the closing assistant
# record (`stop_reason: end_turn` with prose — what #2264 requires before the
# turn may be written). fake-agent.sh's `@transcript` row appends every
# non-comment line to the file named by --transcript, replacing {{NOW}} {{TURN}}
# {{SESSION_ID}} {{CWD}} {{WORKTREE}} {{MESSAGE}} {{EXEC_OUTPUT}} at replay time.
#
# Shape taken from tests/fixtures/claude-transcript-2264/turn-closed.jsonl
# (Claude Code 2.1.240, captured 2026-09-02): the `attachment`, `system` and
# usage bookkeeping are left out because the reader ignores them. The last
# record's text is the Markdown the chat surface renders; the
# `[Header.tsx](src/components/layout/Header.tsx)` link is what becomes a
# ChatFileLink (#2345). No personal path: `cwd` is the seed worktree.
